<title>CANADA: Canadian international travel gap widens in Q3.</title>
<headline>Canadian international travel gap widens in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lower spending by foreign visitors and a slight increase in Canadian spending abroad widened Canada's international travel account deficit by 21.7 percent in the third quarter, Statistics Canada said Friday.</p>
<p>The deficit rose to a seasonally adjusted C$859 million from C$706 million in the second quarter as foreigners spent C$3.72 billion seasonally adjusted, down 4.2 percent from the second-quarter record, and Canadians spent C$2.86 billion, up 0.8 percent.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
